WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
The two studies measure different
outcomes in different settings.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.320
One reports more completed
tasks across field experiments.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:09.360
The other reports longer
completion time for experienced

00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:12.600
developers working
in familiar repositories.

00:00:12.665 --> 00:00:16.080
Neither supplies a universal
quality-engineering savings rate.

00:00:16.256 --> 00:00:20.720
Task mix, developer experience
and verification demands matter.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.520
Use the contrast to design a local
comparison that measures complete work,

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.520
including review and correction, rather
than transferring a headline percentage.
